# The build context is the repository root, but the image builds three Rust
# binaries and nothing else, so only the workspace itself is an input:
# Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, crates/ and vendor/ (russh is a path dependency).
#
# Excluding by allowlist rather than by exception list, because the cost of
# the two mistakes is not the same: a stray directory in the context only
# makes the build slower and invalidates layers when it changes, but a
# missing input fails the build loudly. Everything the image genuinely
# needs is re-included below.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates/
!vendor/

# Build outputs that would otherwise ride along inside those trees. A host
# target/ is both enormous and the wrong architecture.
**/target/
**/.lake/
**/*.rs.bk
